    <briefdescription>
<para>C++20 concept satisfied when a type was accepted by <computeroutput>expect()</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>require()</computeroutput> before the exclusion of the suspicious conditions. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type to be checked.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
Satisfied by the types that are contextually convertible to <computeroutput>bool</computeroutput> but are not <computeroutput>checkable</computeroutput>, i.e. the <computeroutput>suspicious_condition</computeroutput> types. It constrains the deprecated overloads of <computeroutput>expect()</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>require()</computeroutput>, which keep such code compiling for one release, with a warning. </para>
